{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CDs1KTR8knpDijchAXVUcA","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Working notes\n2\t\n3\t## Emoji data and search\n4\t\n5\t- `src/data.ts` is the adapter boundary for the Emoji Mart JSON dataset.\n6\t  Keep the public `EmojiEntry` fields compatible with custom emoji data.\n7\t- `src/search.ts` owns the shared ranking order: name prefix, name\n8\t  substring, then keyword prefix.\n9\t- Changes to the data adapter should be checked with `npm run lint`,\n10\t  `npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json`, and the browser test bundle.\n11\t\n12\t## Picker component conventions\n13\t\n14\t- Picker DOM stays light-DOM; its styles are injected once per document or\n15\t  shadow root through `adoptedStyleSheets`.\n16\t- Picker UI tokens use the `--emoji-picker-*` namespace so host styles can\n17\t  theme the panel without relying on internal class names.\n18\t- Picker category filtering should consume `EmojiEntry.category` or\n19\t  `EmojiEntry.categories`, while text filtering should use `src/search.ts`.\n20\t\n21\t## Component exports\n22\t\n23\t- Public custom elements should register from their component module and keep\n24\t  their DOM in light DOM with styles injected through adopted stylesheets.\n25\t- Adding a public component requires updating the main entrypoint and its\n26\t  explicit package subpath together so ESM and CommonJS builds agree.\n27\t## Picker state and interaction\n28\t\n29\t- Persisted picker preferences should use configurable attributes and guard\n30\t  every `localStorage` read and write with an in-memory fallback.\n31\t- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n32\t  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n33\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b2a073-2dcb-44d7-adf3-864d54401ab0","uuid":"38e6ebbf-a8df-4551-befe-5d0abaf9fd7a","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:45:57.894Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-03-scope-keyboard-handling/AGENTS.md","content":"# Working notes\n\n## Emoji data and search\n\n- `src/data.ts` is the adapter boundary for the Emoji Mart JSON dataset.\n  Keep the public `EmojiEntry` fields compatible with custom emoji data.\n- `src/search.ts` owns the shared ranking order: name prefix, name\n  substring, then keyword prefix.\n- Changes to the data adapter should be checked with `npm run lint`,\n  `npx tsc --noEmit --project tsconfig.json`, and the browser test bundle.\n\n## Picker component conventions\n\n- Picker DOM stays light-DOM; its styles are injected once per document or\n  shadow root through `adoptedStyleSheets`.\n- Picker UI tokens use the `--emoji-picker-*` namespace so host styles can\n  theme the panel without relying on internal class names.\n- Picker category filtering should consume `EmojiEntry.category` or\n  `EmojiEntry.categories`, while text filtering should use `src/search.ts`.\n\n## Component exports\n\n- Public custom elements should register from their component module and keep\n  their DOM in light DOM with styles injected through adopted stylesheets.\n- Adding a public component requires updating the main entrypoint and its\n  explicit package subpath together so ESM and CommonJS builds agree.\n## Picker state and interaction\n\n- Persisted picker preferences should use configurable attributes and guard\n  every `localStorage` read and write with an in-memory fallback.\n- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"totalLines":33}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CfLsGpfcD3y5k61Tp2i1d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UmqHt8kyvUYjVTvAtazZpY","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/nick/code/emoji-input.correctness-audit-fixes-03-scope-keyboard-handling/AGENTS.md","old_string":"- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.","new_string":"- Picker interaction tests should query public roles such as `gridcell`,\n  `radio`, and `status`, rather than component class names or private fields.\n- `renderTabs()` and `renderTones()` replace all children, so any DOM\n  reference grabbed before a click or keydown that triggers re-rendering\n  will be stale. Re-query after the action.\n- Synthetic `KeyboardEvent` dispatches do not trigger native button click\n  behavior in test harnesses. Grid cell Enter/Space must be forwarded to\n  `click()` in the keydown handler; tab and radio Enter/Space rely on\n  the test calling `.click()` after `keydown()` to simulate native\n  behavior.\n- The host `onKeydown` dispatches by `event.target`: grid cells, search\n  input, tabs, and tone radios each have separate handlers. New keyboard\n  controls should follow this dispatch pattern."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":590,"cache_read_input_tokens":79185,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":590},"output_tokens":24,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17b2a073-2dcb-44d7-adf3-864d54401ab0","uuid":"a2b61f05-a55d-4b4e-ae4d-a70525b59311","timestamp":"2026-09-23T18:46:08.608Z","request_id":"req_011CfLsGp8rrVEwEh1Wtfd4